course: dictionary
lesson: 6161
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. The word mind is a good example. «I don't mind waiting» means it's fine with you, not that you are thinking about waiting.
explain: Try swapping a meaning into the sentence. «She has to mind the boys» could mean she must look after them, and that fits. Could it mean she must think about them? It sounds odd, so look after is the better choice.
explain: Some words are used in signs and everyday phrases. In the UK, Ireland and Australia, «Mind the step» is a safety sign that means be careful of the step. Read the words around the sign and you will know what it means.
fact: Your mind is the part of you that thinks, feels, remembers and imagines.
fact: «I don't mind» means it's okay with me.
fact: To mind someone means to look after them, as in «mind your little sister».
fact: «Change your mind» means to decide something different.
fact: «Never mind» means it doesn't matter, and «mind your own business» means don't interfere with other people.
exercise: What does mind mean in «I don't mind waiting»? | *Is fine with it, not annoyed | Remembers how long the wait was | Thinks very hard about the waiting
exercise: «Then she misses her mate's party because she has to mind the boys.» What does mind mean here? | To remember | *To look after | To be careful of | To feel annoyed about
exercise: Which part of you thinks, feels, remembers and imagines? | *Your mind | Your elbow | Your toes
test: «Mind the step» on a train platform means: | Look after the step | Feel annoyed about the steps | *Be careful of the step | Count the steps
test: Which phrase means to decide something different? | Never mind | Peace of mind | Keep in mind | *Change your mind
exam: In «Bump into someone and you say duìbuqǐ; they answer méi guānxi (never mind)», what does never mind mean? | Be careful of the person | *It doesn't matter, no problem | Look after the person | Remember this moment
